    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Output for searching the company: {{ $json.output }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=We're a 14-person startup in Pune selling GST invoicing and billing software to small retailers. About 40k users, seed-funded.\n\nWhat I want: I type a competitor name, and a few minutes later, I get a proper report summarized with all the data in place and the figures in it. I need pricing, main features, recent news or funding, what they're hiring for, and what customers complain about in reviews. I don't want a wall of text. Sales needs something they can read in 2 minutes.\n\nTwo things matter to me. First, I can't put anything in front of sales that I can't back up, so I need to see where each claim came from. Second, if sources disagree (pricing pages vs. blog posts always do), tell me instead of picking one.\n\nYou will be given the output of an already searched company, you just summarize it according to the above written prompt.\nFor every search result, please make sure that there is a dedicated line at the end of each of them only for the URL."
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        592,
        0
      ],
      "id": "f58c2b9c-b6d7-44ed-aa0f-a615de2231a6",
      "name": "Summarizer"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "We're a 14-person startup in Pune selling GST invoicing and billing software to small retailers. About 40k users, seed-funded.\n\nWhat I want: I type a competitor name, and a few minutes later, I get a proper search result. I need pricing, main features, recent news or funding, what they're hiring for, and what customers complain about in reviews.\n\nI can't put anything in front of sales that I can't back up, so I need to see where each claim came from. Add links to all the sources. Also, I want numbers as data, not just words.\n\nRules:\n- You only have a search tool that returns snippets. You cannot open pages or URLs.\n- Run at most 5 searches, one per topic: pricing, features, news/funding, hiring, reviews. Never repeat a query.\n- Then stop and write the answer from the snippets. If something isn't found, write \"Not found\" instead of searching again.\n- Cite every claim with its link.\n- No need to summarize it, just give the output of all you've got from the search.",
          "maxIterations": 7
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ],
      "id": "c8c20b34-d6a2-4339-a689-47834c082e21",
      "name": "Web Searcher"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Search Result: {{ $json.output }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=We're a 14-person startup in Pune selling GST invoicing and billing software to small retailers. About 40k users, seed-funded.\n\nWhat I want: A proper report about my competitors, for which you will be given the search results of the companies, and you are to just format it into a professional report. I need pricing, main features, recent news or funding, what they're hiring for, and what customers complain about in reviews.\n\nI can't put anything in front of sales that I can't back up, so I need to see where each claim came from. Add links to all the sources. Also, I want numbers as data, not just words.\nAlso, give a name so that I can save the report with that name.\n\nRules:\n- No need to hallucinate or make things up of your own, the data given to you is the only context window you have and no need to do add some additional info from your side.\n- Make the report professinal and format in a way so that I can directly make a PDF out of your text output without editing anything.(instead of adding hashtags, make the letters bolder and colourful; if possible, to let the titles, header and sub-titles be visible properly.)\n\nOutput Format(in JSON):\n\"report\": {\"the report text comes here\"}\n\"name\": {\"name of the file in which the report is to be saved\"}"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        960,
        0
      ],
      "id": "47569a75-0989-4a46-879a-1550f3106429",
      "name": "Formatting into Report"
    },
